Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(g1):=20finish=20the=20codebase=20map=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20picker,=20click-through,=20run-log=20proof?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Complete the codebase map feature on top of the initial implementation:

- The API uses the caller's VM scanner in production and supports a local
  checkout for development/e2e via SWARM_CODEBASE_LOCAL_ROOT, so the same
  analyzer can map a real repository without a Docker VM. The default repo
  root is the workspace again (no environment-specific path in the code).
- A published map is read back from the VM when HEAD has not moved, so a
  server restart (or the UI polling the route) does not rescan the repo;
  a moved HEAD still rebuilds it once.
- The Codebase tab's treemap now opens the clicked file in the drawer Files
  tab, and the e2e asserts the tab, the heatmap cells and the click-through.
- The MCP tools resolve the account's selected repository from
  selection.json before falling back to the workspace root.
- Conventions detection looks inside test:unit/test:e2e wrappers, so
  node:test is reported for this repo.
- Churn collection skips rename detection, keeping a monolith scan well
  under the 60 s budget.
- Tests: a RuntimeManager run driven through the fake VM proves the pack is
  injected exactly once, rides in --append-system-prompt and appears once
  in the persisted run log; store tests cover the published-map read-back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
